From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:07:31 -0400
Subject: archive: an Archived view of what auto-archive, Clear and a close
 left behind, restorable to its Space

The sweep and Clear mark the tab they close (auto, clear) and the closed
tab's extra data carries the mark and its Space's name beside the Space id
and folder path it already had, so the recently-closed list is the archive
and shift-cmd-T keeps working; Clear's tabs now join that list. A row above
the switcher opens chrome://stedding-archive, a plain-DOM WebUI page that
groups the closed tabs by day, filters by Space, searches, restores a tab
to its Space (re-creating the Space by name when it is gone) and forgets or
clears entries; the command bar lists matching archived tabs after the open
ones and restores one when chosen; "Keep archived tabs for" (7, 30, 90
days) bounds what the page and the bar show, and the list keeps 500
entries instead of 25 (docs/features/archive.md A7-A11).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-24: Arc's archive, on Chromium's own
list.
Removable when: Chromium's recently-closed list has a page of its own with
workspace membership.
